From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:02:37 +0800
Subject: core/session: say why the provider's safety filter stopped a
 response, with advice

Upstream carries a refusal's category and explanation on the finish reason and
names them. This words it for the user and says what to do, also for a blocked
compaction summary, and falls back to provider metadata (stopDetails, refusal)
for providers that only put it there:

  The provider's safety filter stopped the response (category: cyber): This request was
  declined because it could enable cyber harm. Retrying the same conversation is usually
  stopped again: edit or rephrase your last message, or switch model.

Ocelot-Patch: core/refusal-reason

